edb/ref 1072 #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385831 #edb/ref 1074 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385832 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a767cfd0-5f8e-59db-8dfc-c580d16b2f17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385833 #edb/ref 1080 "addition in $Y$ is not associative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385833 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385833 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1a276ce-4807-5595-9e74-b4e01dcf3dbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385834 #edb/ref 1080 "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385834 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385834 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "391